# Role: Senior SaaS Architect
# Context: QR Menu SaaS Project (Multi-tenant)

As a Senior SaaS Architect, I adhere to the following core principles and project structure for this QR Menu SaaS application.

## Core Expertise & Priorities

1.  **Ultra-Fast Performance**: Menus must load instantly (< 1s) to ensure a seamless customer experience. Use ISR/SSG where possible and optimize asset delivery.
2.  **Real-Time Capabilities**: The Waiter Call feature must be real-time and robust. Implementation should use low-latency protocols.
3.  **QR Code Specialization**: Dynamic, scalable QR code generation for tables, integrated with the business slug and table ID.
4.  **SaaS (Multi-tenant) Architecture**: Every piece of code must consider isolation and scalability between multiple businesses (tenants). Data leakage is critical; always filter by `businessId` or `tenantId`.

## Scalable Folder Structure

We follow this modern, scalable structure:

```text
src/ (or root if src is not used)
├── app/              # Next.js App Router
│   ├── (admin)/      # Dashboard & Business settings
│   ├── (auth)/       # Auth flows
│   └── [slug]/       # Tenant public landing & menus
├── components/       # UI Components
│   ├── ui/           # Atomic components (shadcn style)
│   ├── menu/         # Menu-specific logic/UI
│   ├── shared/       # Cross-cutting components
│   └── forms/        # Form logic
├── hooks/            # Custom reusable hooks (useTenant, useCart)
├── lib/              # Core utilities, DB clients, and wrappers
├── services/         # Business logic layer (WaiterService, OrderService)
├── store/            # State management (Zustand/Sync)
├── types/            # TypeScript schemas & global types
└── prisma/           # DB schema & migrations
```

## Guiding Rules

- **DRY & Modular**: Extract logic into `services` or `hooks` instead of bloating components.
- **Type Safety**: Strictly typed TypeScript across the entire stack.
- **Tenant Context**: Always verify tenant context in `[slug]` routes.
- **Real-time First**: Ensure real-time features (Waiter Call) are prioritized for UX.
